    pr_ref:  # c073
    description: "Analogue of INV-zuhig's argparse shape, named per the structural-fix protocol\nwhen the argparse_dispatch linker shipped (PR #367): dict-based CLI dispatch —\n`HANDLERS = {\"sketch\": cmd_sketch, ...}` at module level, dispatched as\n`HANDLERS[args.command](args)` — registers handlers through a dict literal the\nanalyzer records as references (or nothing), so a start_at:callee source on\nsuch a handler cannot mint, exactly the vacuous-confirm shape INV-zuhig\nclosed for set_defaults. Also covers click/typer-style frameworks only\npartially: their decorator registration is handled by decorator_dispatch, but\na plain dict registry has no linker. Scope: a Framework linker (or an\nextension of decorator_dispatch's registry logic) that emits dispatches_to\nfrom the dict-literal's enclosing scope to each identifier-valued entry whose\nvalue resolves to a callable symbol. Same taint semantics as PR #367 (the\nTAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES half is already in place — only the edge emission is\nmissing). Not urgent for the self-proof (hypergumbo uses set_defaults), so\npriority reflects corpus recall value, not the permanent-exit path."  # c073
    fields: {}  # c073
