  message: "Concrete instance from the 2026-10-06 docstring audit (hypergumbo self-survey, explain): .agent/hooks/_shared/stop_logic.sh:394-396 runs \"$REPO_ROOT/scripts/tracker\" guidance, which reaches hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py _cmd_guidance through the subcommand dispatch; explain _cmd_guidance shows only 'Referenced by main' (cli.py:3837) and no inbound edge from the hook, and generate_guidance shows no non-test production caller beyond _cmd_guidance/generate_guidance_safe. Two hops are missing: shell -> CLI subcommand (bash invoking a repo script by path with a subcommand literal), and subcommand name -> handler (this item). The docstring-staleness playbook (PR #1496) now tells reviewers to grep hooks/scripts/workflows for this reason; closing this item would let explain answer it directly."  # c5d9
